From: ane-stack
Subject: [PATCH 0013] e5rt: explicit state lifecycle (RUN-2)

`state<>` params surface as e5rt inout ports, resident across calls, but that
was implicit: there was no way to inspect, reset, or snapshot state. Adds:

  Program::reset_states()        zero every state port
  Program::state_f16(name)       read a state port as fp16 bits
  Program::state_names()         state ports in bind order
  Program::state_len(name)       element count of one state port
  Program::save_states()         snapshot every port (plain data)
  Program::restore_states(snap)  roll back, validated before any write
  StateSnapshot                  Vec<(String, Vec<u16>)>, no invented format

All operate on the bound buffers execute() reads/writes in place, so a
snapshot round-trip is meaningful. Three E5Error variants added
(NoSuchState, StateSizeMismatch, StateCorrupt) — no exhaustive match on
E5Error existed in the workspace, so this is additive.

Grammar is measured, not assumed. examples/probe_run2_state.rs is a ladder of
five attempts; it establishes that ANE_FRONTEND_SPEC.md line 59 ("accepts any
tensor X") is WRONG for the ANE path and line 281 is right: write_state data
must be the terminal slice_update output. It also establishes that returning
the pre-write read_state value is a valid readback path.

Tests (crates/mil_infer/tests/e5rt.rs): 9 total, all hardware-executed. Each
test compiles into its own cache dir — a shared cache makes them flaky, since
CompileCfg::default() sets force_recompile and concurrent aned runs race the
same e5 bundle cache (measured: 5 of 9 failed before the fix).

